-- test: ADR 0093 rule 6, ADR 0084: the grant of a U3020 carries an edit only when it names `@x` itself or the only binding that permits the requirement; when several do, which one the boundary receives is a decision about trust, so the repair is advice that lists them; at a function value the grant is advice; at an installation the grant is resolved below the installing `with`, so it never names a binding of that `with`; at a call whose statement has a `with` already, the candidates are counted below that `with`, where the added grant resolves, so a header binding that `with` rebinds still counts
-- spec: spec/13 §3
-- expect: error U3020 at src/media/app.una:21:3
-- expect: error U3020 at src/media/app.una:27:3
-- expect: error U3006 at src/media/app.una:32:11
-- expect: error U3020 at src/media/app.una:32:11
-- expect: error U3020 at src/media/app.una:43:44
